Falsifies `periodic_deadline::proofs::a_fire_is_at_least_one_whole_period_on`.

The defect: the first candidate is one nanosecond short of a whole period on,
`prev.saturating_add(period - 1)` in place of `prev.saturating_add(period)`. This is the
inclusive/exclusive slip that writing "the period covers `prev ..= prev + period`" invites, and
it is invisible in the common case, because the snap-back branch below still lands on the beat.
It shows only on the first fire after a registration.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(next_after(prev, period, now) >= prev + period)`, at any
`now` in `prev ..= prev + period - 2`, where the function answers `prev + period - 1` and a
schedule tightens by a nanosecond every time an entry is re-armed.

